---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Pulse Propulsion" description="How to reach light speed using Temporal Decoupling.">
  <article class="container" style="padding-top: 4rem; padding-bottom: 4rem; max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <h1>Temporal Pulse Propulsion</h1>
    <p class="lead">Standard physics says the energy required to reach light speed is infinite. <strong>Temporal Decoupling</strong> says the energy is required to fight <em>time</em>. By pulsing our acceleration, we can reset that friction and conserve energy.</p>

    <!-- Interactive Simulation -->
    <div style="background: #0f172a; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 16px; margin: 2rem 0; text-align: center;">
      
      <canvas id="pulseCanvas" width="600" height="300" style="display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 600px; height: 300px; border: 1px solid #334155; border-radius: 8px; margin: 0 auto; background: #020617;"></canvas>
      
      <div style="margin-top: 1rem; display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <button id="btnStandard" style="padding: 0.5rem 1rem; cursor: pointer; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid #334155; background: #1e293b; color: #fff;">Standard Drive</button>
        <button id="btnPulse" style="padding: 0.5rem 1rem; background: #2563EB; color: white; border: none; cursor: pointer; border-radius: 4px;">Pulse Drive (Theory)</button>
        <button id="btnReset" style="padding: 0.5rem 1rem; cursor: pointer; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid #334155; background: #1e293b; color: #fff;">Reset</button>
      </div>
      <p id="statusText" style="color: #94a3b8; margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.9rem; min-height: 1.5em;">Select a drive mode to compare efficiency.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>The Theory: Grid Compression &amp; Inertial Coasting</h2>
    <p>When a ship accelerates, it pushes against the "tide" of the timeline. This resistance manifests as a compression of the temporal grid. As the grid lines pack closer together, the energy required to maintain thrust increases exponentially.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Standard Drive:</strong> Continuous acceleration compresses the grid relentlessly. The energy cost skyrockets. The ship burns through its fuel supply around the 50% mark, stalls, and coasts to a halt. The compressed grid relaxes as the ship loses momentum.</li>
      <li><strong>Pulse Drive:</strong> Accelerate → Stop (Coast) → Accelerate. During the "Coast" phase, the ship decouples from the timeline flow. The temporal grid <em>spreads back out</em> to normal spacing (zero resistance). Crucially, the ship maintains its high velocity through space, so the relaxed grid lines rush past it. This allows the ship to conserve energy and approach the light barrier asymptotically.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>

  <script is:inline>
    if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
      document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init);
    } else {
      init();
    }

    function init() {
      const canvas = document.getElementById('pulseCanvas');
      if (!canvas) return;
      
      const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
      const btnStandard = document.getElementById('btnStandard');
      const btnPulse = document.getElementById('btnPulse');
      const btnReset = document.getElementById('btnReset');
      const statusText = document.getElementById('statusText');

      let animationId;
      let mode = 'none';
      let shipX = 50;
      let velocity = 0;
      let gridOffset = 0;
      let currentSpacing = 40;
      let energy = 100;

      // TUNING PARAMETERS
      const MAX_SPEED = 4.5;
      const STANDARD_THRUST = 0.35;
      const PULSE_THRUST = 0.45;
      const ACCEL_RATE = 0.08;
      const COAST_DECAY = 0.96; // Standard drive slows down when out of fuel
      const PULSE_COAST_DECAY = 0.9995; // Pulse drive maintains momentum in space (near zero decay)
      const BARRIER_THRESHOLD = 0.95; 

      function getCanvasDimensions() {
        const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
        return { width: rect.width || 600, height: rect.height || 300 };
      }

      function resizeCanvas() {
        const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;
        const { width, height } = getCanvasDimensions();
        canvas.width = width * dpr;
        canvas.height = height * dpr;
        ctx.scale(dpr, dpr);
        canvas.logicalWidth = width;
        canvas.logicalHeight = height;
        draw();
      }

      function draw() {
        const width = canvas.logicalWidth || 600;
        const height = canvas.logicalHeight || 300;
        const lightSpeedLimit = width - 80;

        ctx.clearRect(0, 0, width, height);
        
        // 1. Draw the Dynamic Temporal Grid
        ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;
        
        // Color & glow based on compression
        if (currentSpacing < 12) {
          ctx.shadowBlur = 8;
          ctx.shadowColor = '#ef4444';
          ctx.strokeStyle = '#ef4444';
        } else if (currentSpacing < 22) {
          ctx.shadowBlur = 4;
          ctx.shadowColor = '#f59e0b';
          ctx.strokeStyle = '#f59e0b';
        } else {
          ctx.shadowBlur = 0;
          ctx.strokeStyle = '#334155';
        }

        for (let x = -currentSpacing; x < width; x += currentSpacing) {
          let drawX = (x - gridOffset) % width;
          if (drawX < 0) drawX += width;
          ctx.beginPath();
          ctx.moveTo(drawX, 0);
          ctx.lineTo(drawX, height);
          ctx.stroke();
        }
        ctx.shadowBlur = 0;

        // 2. Draw Light Speed Barrier
        ctx.strokeStyle = '#ef4444';
        ctx.lineWidth = 3;
        ctx.setLineDash([6, 6]);
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.moveTo(lightSpeedLimit, 0);
        ctx.lineTo(lightSpeedLimit, height);
        ctx.stroke();
        ctx.setLineDash([]);
        ctx.fillStyle = '#ef4444';
        ctx.font = 'bold 11px sans-serif';
        ctx.fillText('LIGHT SPEED BARRIER', lightSpeedLimit - 65, 20);

        // 3. Draw Ship
        if (mode !== 'none' || shipX > 50) {
          ctx.fillStyle = '#3b82f6';
          ctx.beginPath();
          ctx.arc(shipX, height / 2, 10, 0, Math.PI * 2);
          ctx.fill();
          
          // Exhaust (only when pushing & has energy)
          let isPushing = (mode === 'standard' && energy > 0) || (mode === 'pulse' && (shipX % 400) < 200 && energy > 0);
          if (isPushing && velocity > 0.1) {
             ctx.fillStyle = '#f59e0b';
             ctx.fillRect(shipX - 15, height/2 - 3, 10, 6);
          }
        }

        // 4. Draw Resistance Bar
        let resistancePercent = 1 - (currentSpacing / 40);
        ctx.fillStyle = '#1e293b';
        ctx.fillRect(10, height - 40, width - 20, 10);
        ctx.fillStyle = resistancePercent > 0.8 ? '#ef4444' : '#10b981';
        ctx.fillRect(10, height - 40, (width - 20) * resistancePercent, 10);
        ctx.fillStyle = '#94a3b8';
        ctx.font = '10px sans-serif';
        ctx.fillText('TEMPORAL RESISTANCE (Grid Density)', 10, height - 45);

        // 5. Draw Energy Bar
        ctx.fillStyle = '#1e293b';
        ctx.fillRect(10, height - 20, width - 20, 10);
        ctx.fillStyle = energy > 30 ? '#3b82f6' : '#ef4444';
        ctx.fillRect(10, height - 20, (width - 20) * (energy / 100), 10);
        ctx.fillStyle = '#94a3b8';
        ctx.fillText('SHIP ENERGY', 10, height - 25);
      }

      function update() {
        const width = canvas.logicalWidth || 600;
        const lightSpeedLimit = width - 80;
        const totalDistance = lightSpeedLimit - 50;
        const progress = (shipX - 50) / totalDistance;

        if (mode === 'standard') {
          let resistance = Math.pow(velocity / MAX_SPEED, 2);
          let energyDrain = 0.25 + (resistance * 1.8); 
          energy -= energyDrain;

          if (energy > 0 && progress < 0.55) {
             let netForce = STANDARD_THRUST - (resistance * 1.2);
             if (netForce > 0) {
                velocity += netForce * ACCEL_RATE;
                shipX += velocity;
                currentSpacing = 40 * (1 - resistance * 0.9);
                statusText.innerText = "Standard Drive: Accelerating. Grid compressing. Energy depleting...";
                statusText.style.color = "#f59e0b";
             } else {
                statusText.innerText = "Standard Drive: Max resistance reached. Energy critical.";
                statusText.style.color = "#ef4444";
             }
          } else {
             if (energy <= 0) energy = 0;
             velocity *= COAST_DECAY; // Slows down to a halt
             shipX += velocity;
             
             currentSpacing += (40 - currentSpacing) * 0.1;
             if (currentSpacing > 39.5) currentSpacing = 40;

             if (progress < 0.5 && energy <= 0) {
                statusText.innerText = "Standard Drive: FUEL DEPLETED. Losing momentum.";
                statusText.style.color = "#ef4444";
             } else if (velocity < 0.1) {
                statusText.innerText = "Standard Drive: Halted. Ship stranded at 50% light speed.";
                statusText.style.color = "#94a3b8";
                mode = 'none';
             }
          }

        } else if (mode === 'pulse') {
           // Longer cycle so you can see the coasting phase clearly
           let cyclePos = shipX % 400; 
           let resistance = Math.pow(velocity / MAX_SPEED, 2);
           
           // Push phase (first 200px of cycle)
           if (cyclePos < 200 && progress < BARRIER_THRESHOLD) {
             if (energy > 0) {
                let netForce = PULSE_THRUST - (resistance * 1.0);
                let energyDrain = 0.12 + (resistance * 0.7);
                energy -= energyDrain;

                if (netForce > 0) {
                   velocity += netForce * ACCEL_RATE;
                   shipX += velocity;
                   currentSpacing = 40 * (1 - resistance * 0.85);
                   statusText.innerText = "Pulse Drive: Accelerating. Grid compressing.";
                   statusText.style.color = "#f59e0b";
                }
             } else {
                cyclePos = 200; // Force coast if out of energy
             }
           } else {
             // Coast phase: Grid resets, but SHIP KEEPS MOVING!
             currentSpacing += (40 - currentSpacing) * 0.15;
             if (currentSpacing > 39.5) currentSpacing = 40;

             // Newton's First Law: Maintain momentum in space
             velocity *= PULSE_COAST_DECAY; 
             shipX += velocity;
             energy -= 0.02; 
             if (energy < 0) energy = 0;
             statusText.innerText = "Pulse Drive: Coasting. Grid relaxed, but momentum maintained!";
             statusText.style.color = "#3b82f6";
           }

           // Asymptotic approach: Never cross the barrier
           if (progress > 0.85) {
              velocity *= 0.97; 
              if (shipX >= lightSpeedLimit - 5) {
                 shipX = lightSpeedLimit - 5;
                 velocity = 0;
                 currentSpacing = 40;
                 statusText.innerText = "Pulse Drive: Threshold reached. Hovering at 99% light speed.";
                 statusText.style.color = "#f59e0b";
                 mode = 'none';
              }
           }
        }

        // Move grid based on ship velocity (This keeps the grid flowing during coast!)
        gridOffset += velocity;

        draw();
        if (mode !== 'none' || velocity > 0.05) {
          animationId = requestAnimationFrame(update);
        }
      }

      btnStandard.addEventListener('click', () => {
        reset();
        mode = 'standard';
        update();
      });

      btnPulse.addEventListener('click', () => {
        reset();
        mode = 'pulse';
        update();
      });

      btnReset.addEventListener('click', reset);

      function reset() {
        mode = 'none';
        shipX = 50;
        velocity = 0;
        gridOffset = 0;
        currentSpacing = 40;
        energy = 100;
        statusText.innerText = "Select a drive mode.";
        statusText.style.color = "#94a3b8";
        draw();
        cancelAnimationFrame(animationId);
      }

      resizeCanvas();
      window.addEventListener('resize', resizeCanvas);
      draw();
    }
  </script>
</BaseLayout>